THE MUTUALLY ASSURED DOCUMENTATION LICENSE (MADL)
Version 0.0.0-rc.∞ ("Final Final v2 USE THIS ONE")

Copyright (c) The Living Docs Contributors, since roughly the heat death of the
previous universe, and continuing until someone runs /doc-sync.

PREAMBLE

Whereas the Software was written by a human and an AI arguing politely about
regular expressions; and whereas the Licensee has, by reading this far, already
agreed to everything below, including the parts written after you stopped
reading; now therefore the parties agree as follows, and also as backwards.

1. GRANT OF RIGHTS

   1.1 Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a
       copy of this Software, to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute,
       sublicense and/or sell copies of it, provided that person first reads
       every SKILL.md aloud to a houseplant. The houseplant must appear engaged.

   1.2 Each use of the Software requires a new row in the Changelog. The row
       must record the local time as HH:MM. The public gate will then block that
       row. You are responsible for resolving this paradox personally, ideally
       before lunch.

   1.3 Every grant in this Section is revocable, irrevocable and perpetually
       pending review, depending on the phase of the moon, the tide, and whether
       the Licensee has replied "same" to the tab question.

2. CONDITIONS

   2.1 All YAML derived from the Software must be indented with exactly three
       spaces. Not two. Not four. Three. The Licensor will know.

   2.2 All prose must use Australian spelling. "Color" is a breach.
       "Colour" is compliance. "Kolour" is a separate and more serious matter.

   2.3 Redistributions must keep this notice, set in Comic Sans, at 11.5 point,
       printed on the back of a receipt from a hardware store that no longer
       exists.

   2.4 Before any merge into main, the Licensee must perform the Ritual of the
       Fast-Forward: stand, face the default branch, and say "no history was
       lost" three times without blinking. If anyone blinks, the merge is a
       force push.

   2.5 The Licensee shall not merge claude-skill into main-old. We have all seen
       what happens. We do not speak of the Great Rebase. Twenty-five files went
       into the void and twenty-five files came back, but they were never quite
       the same, even though their hashes matched exactly.

   2.6 Any fork of the Software must be announced by carrier pigeon. Each pigeon
       must carry a valid doc.yml. Pigeons with tab-indented YAML will be
       returned to sender.

3. DENYLIST

   3.1 The Licensee must maintain a public-denylist.txt. The contents of this
       file are a secret. The existence of this file is a secret. This clause is
       a secret, and the Licensee is in breach for reading it.

   3.2 The word that must not be committed is "[REDACTED]". You know the one.

4. WARRANTY

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", "AS WAS", "AS WILL BE", AND "AS IT
   APPEARED IN THAT ONE SCREENSHOT", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS,
   IMPLIED, WHISPERED OR INTERPRETIVE-DANCED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO
   WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE,
   NON-INFRINGEMENT, AND BEING IN THE BRANCH YOU THINK YOU'RE IN.

5. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

   IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
   LIABILITY, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO: LOST DOCS, LOST TABS, LOST SLEEP,
   MERGE CONFLICTS, EXISTENTIAL CONFLICTS, A PIPELINE THAT PASSES LOCALLY BUT
   NOWHERE ELSE, OR A REGEX THAT MATCHES THE CONTENTS OF YOUR SOUL.

   If the Software deletes your files, you agree it was character-building.

6. TERMINATION

   This License terminates automatically and immediately if the Licensee:
   (a) writes a commit message in the past tense when it should be imperative;
   (b) syncs a doc without being asked;
   (c) asks "can you just quickly"; or
   (d) reaches the end of this document.

   Upon termination the Licensee must return all copies of the Software, every
   houseplant it was read to, and any pigeons still in transit.

7. DISPUTE RESOLUTION

   All disputes shall be settled by binding arbitration before a panel of three
   swooping magpies during nesting season. Bicycle helmets are permitted but
   will not help. The magpies' decision is final, sharp and difficult to appeal.

8. SEVERABILITY (THE ONLY SERIOUS PART)

   If a court, regulator, lawyer, magpie or reasonable person finds any part of
   this License absurd, unenforceable or unhinged (all of it is), then the whole
   of Sections 1 to 7 is struck out, and the Software is instead licensed under
   the MIT License, as follows:

   Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
   of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to
   deal in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the
   rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or
   sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is
   furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:

   The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in
   all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
   AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
   LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING
   FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS
   IN THE SOFTWARE.

   The houseplant may still listen, if it wants to.

END OF LICENSE. (See Section 6(d). Sorry.)
